mapping.signal:
The observable is the structure of the residuals across path classes, not their overall size.

Pattern expected if a deployed change is responsible:
- residuals concentrate on paths that cross one changed cell;
- they scale roughly with the number of traversals of that cell;
- they persist within matched load strata, including low load;
- they are near zero on paths that bypass the cell under the same load and time window;
- onset on each host or instance aligns with when that instance received the change, not with a shift in traffic level.

Pattern expected if load variation is responsible:
- residuals track the load covariates across all paths sharing the loaded resource, whether or not they cross a changed cell;
- they appear on instances still running the old version;
- they shrink or vanish when compared within matched load strata.

Mixed pattern: residuals appear only on paths crossing a changed cell but grow with load. This indicates a change in load sensitivity rather than a fixed added delay.

Unstructured residuals: no organisation by path or by load indicates measurement noise or a missing model component.

Additional observables:
- the recovered location and magnitude of the synthetic delay in the resolution test;
- how much the fitted increments move when regularisation is varied;
- for the follow-up interventions, whether the residual disappears and returns with the change at held load.
